                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Ghost Song is not my favorite metroidvania. The combat is not that fun and the exploration is not as rewarding and as rich as you can find in other games of the genre.\n\nHowever, what Ghost Song is amazing at is providing you with a genuinely touching story about people finding comfort in each other when going through tragedies. The dicussions you are able to have with the survivors of the crash are some of the most beautiful moments of intimacy and quiet I've had in gaming. \n\nIt feels very sad to see people who are trying to keep themselves together but are shattered enough to try to establish a bond with our stern mechanical suit, but you are able to see these people process their trauma and lean on each other.\n\nI really liked it for what it was.",
